1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:21,539
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June twelfth. Tokyo's stock market had a huge day — Japan's main stock index jumped more than twenty-five hundred yen at one point, after an announcement from Washington eased fears about a conflict in the Middle East. Let's listen.

2
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:24,899
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:34,984
[News] 6月12日、東京の株式市場で、日経平均株価が大きく上がりました。

4
00:00:35,683 --> 00:00:43,820
[News] 株価は、前の日に比べて、一時2500円以上高くなりました。

5
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:50,496
[News] 理由は、アメリカのトランプ大統領の発表です。

6
00:00:51,195 --> 00:01:02,716
[News] トランプ大統領は11日、予定していたイランへの攻撃を中止したと、自分のSNSで明らかにしました。

7
00:01:03,415 --> 00:01:12,296
[News] 戦いが終わるかもしれないという期待から、世界の市場に安心感が広がりました。

8
00:01:12,995 --> 00:01:20,195
[News] アメリカの市場では、半導体の会社の株が大きく上がりました。

9
00:01:20,896 --> 00:01:29,487
[News] 東京の市場でも、半導体に関係する会社の株を買う動きが強まりました。

10
00:01:30,188 --> 00:01:38,084
[News] 日経平均株価は、一時6万6800円くらいまで上がりました。

11
00:01:38,784 --> 00:01:48,408
[News] 専門家は、「中東の状況を、これからも注意して見る必要があります」と話しています。

12
00:01:49,108 --> 00:01:50,739
[Host] Let's break it down.

13
00:01:51,340 --> 00:02:02,067
[Slow] 6月12日、東京の株式市場で、日経平均株価が大きく上がりました。

14
00:02:02,867 --> 00:02:08,795
[Host] On June twelfth, on the Tokyo stock market, Japan's main stock index rose sharply.

15
00:02:09,395 --> 00:02:11,580
[Vocab] 株価

16
00:02:11,979 --> 00:02:19,900
[Host] It means stock price. The first character means stock, the second means price — you'll hear it in every market report.

17
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:29,788
[Slow] 株価は、前の日に比べて、一時2500円以上高くなりました。

18
00:02:30,587 --> 00:02:37,307
[Host] Compared with the previous day, the index was at one point more than twenty-five hundred yen higher.

19
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:40,139
[Vocab] 一時

20
00:02:40,539 --> 00:02:48,795
[Host] It means for a time, or at one point. News stories love this word — it says something happened briefly, not all day.

21
00:02:49,395 --> 00:02:56,235
[Slow] 理由は、アメリカのトランプ大統領の発表です。

22
00:02:57,036 --> 00:03:00,659
[Host] The reason was an announcement from the American president.

23
00:03:01,259 --> 00:03:03,683
[Vocab] 発表

24
00:03:04,084 --> 00:03:12,843
[Host] It means announcement, making something public. Companies, governments, even students presenting in class all use this word.

25
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:26,620
[Slow] トランプ大統領は11日、予定していたイランへの攻撃を中止したと、自分のSNSで明らかにしました。

26
00:03:27,419 --> 00:03:34,548
[Host] On the eleventh, the president revealed on his own social media that he had called off a planned attack on Iran.

27
00:03:35,147 --> 00:03:37,475
[Vocab] 中止

28
00:03:37,876 --> 00:03:46,156
[Host] It means cancellation — stopping something that was planned. Rained-out fireworks, cancelled events, and here, a called-off attack.

29
00:03:46,756 --> 00:03:56,907
[Slow] 戦いが終わるかもしれないという期待から、世界の市場に安心感が広がりました。

30
00:03:57,707 --> 00:04:03,108
[Host] Hopes that the fighting might end spread a sense of relief through markets around the world.

31
00:04:03,707 --> 00:04:05,819
[Vocab] 期待

32
00:04:06,219 --> 00:04:13,252
[Host] It means expectation or hope — looking forward to something good. Markets run on exactly this feeling.

33
00:04:13,852 --> 00:04:22,084
[Slow] アメリカの市場では、半導体の会社の株が大きく上がりました。

34
00:04:22,884 --> 00:04:27,923
[Host] In the American market, shares of semiconductor companies rose sharply.

35
00:04:28,524 --> 00:04:31,091
[Vocab] 半導体

36
00:04:31,492 --> 00:04:41,620
[Host] It means semiconductor — the chips inside phones and computers. The first character means half, because these materials half-conduct electricity.

37
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:52,036
[Slow] 東京の市場でも、半導体に関係する会社の株を買う動きが強まりました。

38
00:04:52,836 --> 00:04:58,500
[Host] In Tokyo too, the move to buy shares of chip-related companies grew stronger.

39
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,331
[Vocab] 動き

40
00:05:01,732 --> 00:05:11,740
[Host] It means movement or trend. It comes from the verb to move, and news Japanese uses it for what investors, politicians, or whole countries are doing.

41
00:05:12,339 --> 00:05:23,331
[Slow] 専門家は、「中東の状況を、これからも注意して見る必要があります」と話しています。

42
00:05:24,132 --> 00:05:28,980
[Host] Experts say the situation in the Middle East still needs to be watched carefully.

43
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:32,028
[Vocab] 状況

44
00:05:32,427 --> 00:05:40,396
[Host] It means situation — how things stand right now. A very common word in news, business, and everyday check-ins.

45
00:05:40,995 --> 00:05:43,995
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

46
00:05:44,596 --> 00:05:47,355
[News] 今日のニュースです。

47
00:05:48,055 --> 00:05:57,439
[News] 6月12日、東京の株式市場で、日経平均株価が大きく上がりました。

48
